From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denfry <dabinayo@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:28:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Make the player name map thread-safe

playersByUUID is already a ConcurrentHashMap, but playersByName is still
a HashMap, while players join and leave on different region threads and
plugins look players up by name from any region.

Based on PaperMC/Folia#497 (Dueris)

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java b/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
index 82fb4aecffaf4ae97a9c2ab60eca2d67107de0a8..5869785258d2ec7483ed11275f4abc072068e74b 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
@@ -134,7 +134,7 @@ public abstract class PlayerList {
 
     // CraftBukkit start
     private org.bukkit.craftbukkit.CraftServer cserver;
-    private final Map<String,ServerPlayer> playersByName = new java.util.HashMap<>();
+    private final Map<String,ServerPlayer> playersByName = new java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap<>(); // Tessera - regions add and remove players concurrently
     public @Nullable String collideRuleTeamName; // Paper - Configurable player collision
 
     // Folia start - region threading
